      {
        "id": 201461,
        "name": "schadkehnfreude",
        "username": "schadkehnfreude",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/schadkehnfreude/{size}/2357_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-15T14:40:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Belatedly... I got a near-mint that shoulda been a mint (mis-clicked and rewound because it was a pretty crucial mis-click), but yes, this one is a bear. &nbsp;This was the key for me:</p><p><em><span>I'd suggest having Parse switch to deck control as soon as possible and prioritizing destroying Mable and La Paradoja Magnifica first. Also, I got a lot of use out of Writhe's Caliginous Form, Sentinels Tactics, and Exploit Vulnerability.</span></em></p><p>Generally, the first few turns were just holding on for dear life and burning down Mable and then the ship with extreme prejudice. &nbsp;I didn't switch to deck control until I'd stablized because I was trying to get the team set-up. &nbsp;At some point early in the game, the Sentinels have that Mainstay ongoing that tanks damage - you should be able to keep it up for two turns: &nbsp;that, in addition to his DR power and his signature should buy you the time you need to stablize. &nbsp;Unity mostly recycled Bee-bot, which was helpful. &nbsp;I got a bit lucky when the environment played everybody's cards - Maria got the guy who zaps at start of turn for X = number of hero toys, which at that point was 13+, but Expatty got Flak Jacket in the same play, which absorbed the hit.</p><p>Hairtrigger and Exploit Vulnerability were the low-key MVPs but you gotta survive the initial blitz of all the pirates first.</p>",
