        "id": 201462,
        "name": "QuirkyDM",
        "username": "QuirkyDM",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/quirkydm/{size}/2033_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-08-31T18:51:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had a heck of a time with this one, too. I took down Mabel and the ship ASAP, but I found I couldn't get the rest of the crew under control and La Capitan wasn't being touched. At the end, I used Parse and Writhe for a little bit of card control, but then decided to forego damage mitigation, ignore the rest of the crew and just hit back hard. Phosphorescent Fungus + Targeting Arrow gave +2 damage to all my attacks for a turn. With everyone focused on attacks, I did 40+ damage to La Capitan in that turn and weathered the next turn of attacks to finish her off next turn with Mr. Chompy. I'm more of a slow play, lock up the game sort of player, but sometimes you just have to just punch your way through the problem.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
